      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-63401",
      ":question/problem": "Samantha was walking in the forest with her friends. Every hour they recorded their coordinates on a map using a GPS navigator. Their results are given in the table below. The coordinates that she records are set up so that a difference of one unit corresponds to one kilometer.\n\n| Time | Coordinates |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $1$ pm | $(-2, 0)$ |\n| $2$ pm | $(-2,-2)$ |\n| $3$ pm | $(3,-2)$ |\n| $4$ pm | $(3, 2)$ |\n| $5$ pm | $(0, 4)$ |\n\nAssuming that they traveled at a constant speed from $2$ pm to $3$ pm, what was their speed during this time interval?"
    }
